Figure 1. Absolute error of the composite trapezoidal (circles) and Simpson (squares) rules for the integral of exp(x) sin(3x) over [0, 2] against n, log-log axes, n = 4..4096. Solid lines are the ordinary least-squares fits of ln(error) on ln(n) over the points with error > 1e-13 (trapezoidal: n = 4..4096, slope -2.001080, 95% interval [-2.002078, -2.000083]; Simpson: n = 4..2048, slope -3.893577, 95% interval [-4.017581, -3.769572]; the Simpson n = 4096 error, open square, lies below the threshold and is not fitted). Dashed grey lines are guides of slope -2 and -4, shifted up 4x from the fits for visibility; only their slope is meaningful. Source: experiment-repo results/errors.csv and results/fits.json at f537049ac52de0cbc289a9aa5e8c3f727b5ad833; generator report/figures/make_figure.py.
